From: Chimera core
Subject: [PATCH] a block file can be written into a stream

With SUPERMODEL_CHIMERA, a block file (Supermodel's NVRAM and savestate
format) can be written into a stream the caller opened, as well as into
a file it names. The Chimera core writes the game's NVRAM file (its
EEPROM and backup RAM, as upstream's NVRAM/<game>.nv holds them) into
its own memory for Emulator > Export Save Data: the sandbox has no
folder to write to.
---
--- a/Src/BlockFile.h
+++ b/Src/BlockFile.h
@@ -206,6 +206,17 @@
    */
   Result Create(const std::string &file, const std::string &headerName, const std::string &comment);
 
+#ifdef SUPERMODEL_CHIMERA
+  /*
+   * Create(stream, headerName, comment):
+   *
+   * The same, into a stream the caller opened (the Chimera core writes the
+   * NVRAM file into its own memory: the sandbox has no folder to write to).
+   * Close() closes the stream.
+   */
+  Result Create(FILE *stream, const std::string &headerName, const std::string &comment);
+#endif
+
